      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not an air quality sensor.\n2: MATCH 1 -- Both specify a desired temperature.\n3: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not a condensing unit.\n4: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not a heat exchanger.\n5: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not a humidifier.\n6: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not an isolation valve.\n7: NO MATCH -- A setpoint is not a dry cooler.",
      "relationships": "1: MATCH 6 -- Having a fan expresses the part relationship.\n2: MATCH 7 -- Having a filter expresses the part relationship.\n3: MATCH 8 -- Having a damper expresses the part relationship.\n4: MATCH 10 -- Having a cooling valve expresses the part relationship.\n5: MATCH 9 -- Having a heating valve expresses the part relationship.\n6: MATCH 11 -- Having an economizer expresses the part relationship.\n7: MATCH 15 -- Both associate the air handling unit with an air temperature sensor point.\n8: MATCH 16 -- Both associate the air handling unit with an air temperature setpoint.\n9: MATCH 17 -- Both associate the air handling unit with a cooling temperature setpoint.\n10: MATCH 18 -- Both associate the air handling unit with a heating temperature setpoint.\n11: MATCH 19 -- Both associate the air handling unit with a temperature deadband setpoint.\n12: MATCH 5 -- Both associate the thermostat with its temperature sensor input.\n13: MATCH 12 -- Both associate the zone with an occupancy sensor.\n14: MATCH 22 -- Installation in the building specifies the sensor’s location.\n15: MATCH 1 -- Containing a floor expresses the part relationship.\n16: MATCH 3 -- Containing a space expresses the part relationship.\n17: MATCH 2 -- Containing a zone expresses the part relationship.\n18: MATCH 20 -- Both associate the air handling unit with an outside air CO2 sensor point.\n19: MATCH 21 -- Both associate the air handling unit with a return air CO2 sensor point.",
      "properties": "1: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured temperature.\n2: NO MATCH -- A reading is not the sensor's status.\n3: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured air temperature.\n4: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured CO2 level.\n5: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured outside-air CO2 level.\n6: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured return-air CO2 level.\n7: NO MATCH -- A generic reading does not clearly denote the occupied flag.\n8: MATCH \"condition\" -- A filter's status describes its condition.\n9: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured CO2 differential.\n10: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured water temperature.",
